Half Dugout
A primitive shelter, often temporary, 
having a significant portion of its 
structure dug below ground level; 
commonly has sod walls and a sod roof; 
also see sod house.

Such buildings 
are often characterized by front-facing 
gables that rise above the roofline; 
elaborate brickwork or stonework; 
quoins at the corners of the building; 
occasionally, turrets or towers; stone 
straight-line gables or multicurved 
gables, tall decorative chimneys; 
rectangular window frames, usually 
containing small, leaded panes of glass 
set in casement sashes.

Liner Plate
A prefabricated plate of stamped steel; 
has corrugations to provide stiffness; 
provided with flanges so that similar 
units can be bolted together to form a 
support system for a tunnel, shaft, or pit.

